---
/**
 * The page-level affiliate disclosure.
 *
 * Under MkDocs this partial was included by hand on 29 pages, which means it
 * could be forgotten, reordered, or moved above the content it is disclosing.
 * As a component it renders identically everywhere.
 *
 * This is now the only place the arrangement is stated in full — see the note
 * in BuyOptions.astro about why the sentence no longer repeats per block. It
 * reads as a quiet closing note rather than a bordered panel, because it sits
 * at the foot of the article where nothing is competing for attention anyway.
 */
---

<aside class="disclosure" aria-label="Affiliate disclosure">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="currentColor">
    <path d="M21.41 11.58l-9-9A2 2 0 0 0 11 2H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v7a2 2 0 0 0 .59 1.42l9 9a2 2 0 0 0 2.82 0l7-7a2 2 0 0 0 0-2.84zM6.5 8A1.5 1.5 0 1 1 8 6.5 1.5 1.5 0 0 1 6.5 8z" />
  </svg>
  <p>
    Links marked with a tag are affiliate links. If you buy through one we may earn a
    small commission, <strong>at no extra cost to you</strong>. Commissions pay for
    hosting and never influence what we recommend — see the{' '}
    <a href="/policies/">editorial policy</a>.
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .disclosure {
    display: flex;
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-block: var(--space-6);
    padding-block-start: var(--space-3);
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .disclosure svg {
    flex: none;
    margin-block-start: 0.32em;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .disclosure p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .disclosure strong {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .disclosure a {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
</style>
